## Root cause

The root cause of the incident was a DNS outage at the upstream provider. This 
caused the payments database connection pool to become exhausted, leading to 
multiple 503 errors for tenants `acme-retail`, `northwind`, and `globex`.

## Customer impact

- Tenant `acme-retail` experienced multiple failed requests to `/v1/charges`.
- Tenant `northwind` experienced multiple failed requests to `/v1/charges`.
- Tenant `globex` experienced multiple failed requests to `/v1/charges`.

